-- statement:
--   **The sweep over the axes computes `pipeSweep`** (general axis step `pf`).
--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `Solutions.J6SegILSweep9`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem J6Seg.sweep_runF {Pp : ℕ} {Isym : List Sym} {tbl : Fin Pp → IStmt HS Pp} {eX : Fin Pp}
--       {σ : Fin 19 → Fin HS} {dS dA : Fin HS} (hW : SwOK σ dS dA)
--       {P : Prm} {n : ℕ} {src : ℕ → ℕ} {D : ℕ} {Cx : ℝ} {pf : ℕ → List GI → List GI}
--       (hX : AxisBodyF P n src D pf Isym tbl eX dA Cx) (hCx : 0 ≤ Cx) (hD : dP6 P n = D + 1)
--       (B : ℕ) (hb : SwB P n src D B)
--       (Q : List GI → Prop) (hQ : ∀ L, Q L → L.length = TW P n D ∧ GB (pP6 P n + 2) L)
--       (hpipe : ∀ k ≤ D, ∀ L : List GI, Q L → Q (pf k L))
--       (s : IState HS) (f : Fin HS → List ℤ) (l : List ℤ)
--       (hf : ∀ j, j ≠ 0 → j ≠ dS → f j = []) (hdesc : f dS = descLine6 P n src)
--       (ys : List GI) (h0 : f 0 = gflat ys ++ l) (hys : Q ys) :
--       ∃ c : ℕ, IRuns Isym tbl (swp σ dS dA eX) (encK s f)
--           (encK s (update f 0 (gflat (pipeSweep (pf) (D + 1) ys) ++ l))) c ∧
--         (c : ℝ) ≤ (D + 1) * (Cx + 10 ^ 9 * (B + 2) ^ 2) + 10 ^ 9 * (B + 2) ^ 2 * (D + 2)
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** B-line IL, B6: **`sweep_run`** (the sweep over the axes computes `pipeSweep`)
--
--   `swp σ dS dA eX = hdrA; swL; hdrC`: read the line descriptor `descLine6` on `dS` (header to
--   registers, bits counted, `T`), loop over the axes `k = 0..D` (axis descriptor `descAx6` on `dA`,
--   call `eX`), restore the descriptor (`hdrC`: move the used `s`'s and bits back, push
--   `d, h, α, p`, clear the registers).
--
--   **`sweep_run`**: on a state with `dS = descLine6 P n src` and every other managed stack except
--   `0` empty, with `ys` (length `∏ t`, `GB (p+2)`) on stack `0`, given `AxisBody6 … eX dA Cx` and the
--   list invariant of `pipe6`, `swp` leaves `gflat (pipeSweep (pipe6 P n src D) (D+1) ys) ++ l` on
--   stack `0`, everything else unchanged, at cost `(D+1)(Cx + 10^9 (B+2)^2) + 10^9 (B+2)^2 (D+2)`.
--
